253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (A computer vision system should first be introduced to support manual inspection rather than immediately replace it. Industrial cameras and Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) models could continuously identify visible defects, reducing the effect of worker fatigue and providing an additional quality check. The CCA-YOLO model, developed for nitrile medical gloves, achieved mean Average Precision \(mAP\) above 99% for several tear and scratch defects. Commercial systems have also demonstrated high-speed automated glove inspection.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
