/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (AI should not be used as the sole basis for decisions where a guaranteed pass or fail result is required. Machine learning systems operate using probabilities and confidence levels, which are not suitable for critical safety decisions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (The existing pinhole and voltage leak tests should therefore remain deterministic and rule-based, particularly for medical, electrical, and other high-risk gloves. AI can instead be used to support areas such as surface defect detection, process prediction, and early identification of production problems.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (Overall, the AIoT layer should act as the final stage of the proposed roadmap. By combining reliable data from quality control, packaging, mixing, and other production stages, DPL could move from simply recording production information to using it for predictive and better-informed decisions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
