/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Computer vision should be considered the first major automation investment because it directly addresses the risk of fatigue during manual inspection. Its main benefit would be the addition of a consistent inspection layer rather than the immediate replacement of inspectors.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Industry applications have shown that AI-based vision systems can operate at high production speeds and detect defects that may be difficult to identify consistently through manual inspection. The investment could therefore be justified through improved quality consistency, reduced rework, and lower risk of defective products reaching customers.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
