302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (The next investment should focus on automated counting and digital verification rather than full robotic packaging. DPL handles more than 100 pack types with different folding methods, logos, artwork, and box formats, making complete packaging automation difficult to justify immediately.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Automated counting systems can improve quantity accuracy, while barcode verification can ensure that the correct product is matched with the relevant order. Industry solutions have already combined automated counting, cartoning, and barcode verification in glove manufacturing.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (For DPL, counting and digital verification should first be introduced for high-volume and standardised pack types. This would provide measurable improvements without requiring the entire packaging process to be automated at once. Full robotic packaging could be considered later where sufficient standardisation exists.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
